For visible prose, mapped printed Cyrillic a/b/etc. labels in source order to Latin a/b/etc., removed whitespace only, and compared every complete exercise string. The sole non-layout exception was the single registered 707a replacement of $y=ca$ by $y=ca^x$. All other normalized visible characters agree. Also independently extracted all 188 $...$ formula strings in order and compared them completely, allowing only that 707a replacement: no other formula difference. Final local verification returned exit 0 and confirmed unchanged byte hashes for all four whitelist inputs, all 127 visible labels beginning separate lines in natural Latin order, source.data exact equality and the one attachment owner 690.

